# 59. Quick Interview Revision – Defect Management

## Important Definitions

| Term           | Meaning                                         |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Defect         | Difference between expected and actual behavior |
| Severity       | Impact of defect                                |
| Priority       | Urgency to fix                                  |
| Retesting      | Verify a specific defect fix                    |
| Regression     | Verify existing functionality after changes     |
| Blocker        | Prevents testing/progress                       |
| Defect Leakage | Defect escapes to later environment             |
| Defect Triage  | Review and prioritize defects                   |
| RCA            | Identify root cause                             |
| Defect Aging   | Time defect remains open                        |
| Reopen         | Defect fails validation after fix               |
| Duplicate      | Already reported issue                          |
| Deferred       | Fix postponed                                   |
| Rejected       | Issue is not accepted as a defect               |

---

# 60. Best Senior QA Interview Answer Pattern

For almost any defect scenario, use this structure:

```text
1. Understand the issue
2. Reproduce the issue
3. Collect evidence
4. Validate the requirement
5. Assess severity
6. Assess business impact
7. Create/document the defect
8. Discuss during triage
9. Support investigation
10. Retest the fix
11. Perform targeted regression
12. Verify and close
13. Analyze root cause
14. Add preventive coverage
```

## Golden Rule

> **Never treat defect management as simply "logging bugs."**

A strong QA engineer manages the complete quality risk:

```text
Detect
  ↓
Analyze
  ↓
Communicate
  ↓
Prioritize
  ↓
Validate Fix
  ↓
Regression
  ↓
Prevent Recurrence
```

