# Interview Tip

When answering scenario-based questions, avoid answers such as:

> "I will create a Jira ticket."

That sounds like a junior-level answer.

Instead say:

> "I would first reproduce and validate the issue, assess the business and technical impact, collect supporting evidence, document the defect clearly, discuss the priority during triage, validate the fix, perform targeted regression, and finally analyze the root cause to prevent recurrence."

That demonstrates **Senior QA / SDET-level ownership**.

